{
  "_note": "Every unit of the Reader Artifacts Handbook with one disposition, so the board can say how much of it is filed, landed, deferred or declined. Written by hand; tools/check.mjs fails when a spec row, operation, rule, proposal, verification check, declined item, taste item or handbook story is missing here or listed twice, when a key is not a board row, or when a story's card does not name the units it closes. Status is never written here: tools/coverage.mjs reads it from the fleet board. Dispositions: story (filed; keys), existing (an earlier board story; keys), applied (Marxy already does it), partial (keys for the part filed, bundle for the rest), deferred (v1.1; bundle), declined (reason in note), default (a taste item shipped at the research default; keys carry the queue row).",
  "bundles": {
    "v1.1-operations": "The artifact operations catalogue (docs/scope.md: operations beyond the four are v1.1): copy-source, copy-command, copy-diff-after/before, extract-*, JSON copy/format/minify, strip-ansi, copy-front-matter, invisible-character strip/escape/copy. One story per family when v1.1 opens; ADR-0036 clause 8 makes each an additive registration.",
    "v1.1-provenance": "Anchors and lenses over byte provenance: P04 (OperationInput.source), P09 (anchor on the reading position), copy-with-reference, copy-anchor, changed-since-last-read with a core histogram diff, the data-fence depth lens, the reveal-hidden lens, the front-matter hide toggle. Needs P04 and P09 re-proposed as ADRs.",
    "v1.1-transcript": "The derived JSONL transcript view (P10): turns, speaker labels, bounded tool output, thinking behind a click, and the transcript copy operations. The most invasive proposal; after the cheaper stories and a taste review of the Source view.",
    "v1.1-readme-extras": "Emoji shortcodes from a bundled MIT table."
  },
